## Integration Patterns

### QML-C++ Integration
```cpp
// Service exposure in QGroundControlQmlGlobal.h
Q_PROPERTY(MissionService* missionService READ missionService CONSTANT)

// QML usage
Connections {
    target: QGroundControl.missionService
    enabled: QGroundControl.missionService !== null
    function onMissionGenerationStarted() { /* ... */ }
}
```

### Service Dependencies
```cpp
// MissionService constructor
MissionService::MissionService(QObject* parent) : QObject(parent)
{
    m_ptahMissionGenerator = new PtahMissionGenerator(this);
    m_missionUploadService = new MissionUploadService(this);
    m_vehicleService = new VehicleService(this);
    
    // Connect signals
    connect(m_vehicleService, &VehicleService::vehiclesReady, 
            this, &MissionService::onVehiclesReady);
    connect(m_missionUploadService, &MissionUploadService::missionUploadCompleted,
            this, &MissionService::onMissionUploadCompleted);
}
```

## Error Handling Architecture

### Error Propagation Pattern
```
QML Layer:
  ┌─────────────────┐
  │ Error Dialog    │ ◄─── Error Messages
  └─────────────────┘
              ▲
              │
Service Layer:
  ┌─────────────────┐
  │ Error Handling  │ ◄─── Validation & Recovery
  │ & Logging       │
  └─────────────────┘
              ▲
              │
Generator Layer:
  ┌─────────────────┐
  │ Input Validation│ ◄─── Parameter Checking
  │ & Error Returns │
  └─────────────────┘
```

### Error Handling Strategies
```cpp
// Service layer error handling
void MissionService::generateMission(const QString& missionType, 
                                   int areaSize, 
                                   int altitude, 
                                   int speed, 
                                   const QString& description)
{
    // Input validation
    if (areaSize <= 0 || altitude <= 0) {
        emit missionGenerationCompleted(false, "Invalid parameters");
        return;
    }
    
    // Vehicle validation
    Vehicle* activeVehicle = MultiVehicleManager::instance()->activeVehicle();
    if (!activeVehicle) {
        emit missionGenerationCompleted(false, "No active vehicle");
        return;
    }
    
    // Proceed with generation
    // ...
}
```

## Memory Management Patterns

### QObject Parent-Child Relationships
```cpp
// Automatic cleanup through parent-child relationships
MissionService::MissionService(QObject* parent) : QObject(parent)
{
    // Children will be automatically deleted when parent is destroyed
    m_ptahMissionGenerator = new PtahMissionGenerator(this);
    m_missionUploadService = new MissionUploadService(this);
    m_vehicleService = new VehicleService(this);
}
```

### Smart Pointer Usage
```cpp
// Use QPointer for safe object access
QPointer<Vehicle> m_activeVehicle;

void MissionService::setActiveVehicle(Vehicle* vehicle)
{
    m_activeVehicle = vehicle;
}

void MissionService::useActiveVehicle()
{
    if (m_activeVehicle) {
        // Safe to use - object still exists
        QGeoCoordinate pos = m_activeVehicle->coordinate();
    }
}
```

